      "writtenOn": "2024-12-09T12:29:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "load_balance() tends to hold the two rqs when it migrates tasks. I\u0027m not sure if we can end up with races with load_balance() tries to do something with this task too.\n\nI assume this path can never trigger for a running task right? You intercept the wake up path to force the migration before we enqueue it. Just double checking.\n\nWhat about migrate_disable() sections? Seems out of the scope of this patch, but beside affinity, a task might need to stay on an CPU because it is on migrate_disable() section so we need to ensure it moves back to that CPU when it wakes up.\n\n(sorry have\u0027t looked at later patches yet if this is handled later)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 6886,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 6887,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "498de7c6984ee0a65d5923f4ee4bea20dc7353fe",
